# R22: Narrator lines for the Crooked Nightmare (region crooked_nightmare: nm_estate, nm_estate_ruins and the eight dreams nm_pit to nm_attic). The Narrator is the
# Vagrant, telling the tale afterwards: second person, present tense, one or two sentences, no game words. In the dream his humour comes back a little,
# the way a ferryman jokes in a storm. The dream's rules: you cannot walk out of a scene, doors are crooked and glow red inside, the moon wanes from full
# to half to new, and anything that laughs changes the rules. No {name} or {target} in a plain line (those are not voiced). Written by hand; new lines are
# fine, unvoiced until the voice thread records them.

~ enter:nm_estate
| The hill road is the same, and the house at the top of it is not. Every line of it has been bent again, and a window flashes red, then black.
| Purple slime runs down the clapboard like a cheap sauce, and from somewhere inside, people are screaming in the polite way of folk who have been screaming a while.
cooldown 30

~ enter:nm_estate_ruins
| Where the house stood there is a heap, and over the heap the freed spirits turn in the clean starlight like wasps round a broken hive.
| The air is quiet and cold and finally honest. Nothing in the rubble is crooked, because nothing in it is standing.
cooldown 30

~ enter:nm_pit
| There is no floor, and no up. The walls of a wet earthen shaft go past, and the attic's boards hang far above in the wreckage like a lid you will not be put back under.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_dark_wood
| A full moon with no face on it, and a wood of beech and hickory gone blue and grey. Small white handprints show on the trunks at every turn.
| Leaves crackle underfoot in the way leaves do only when something is listening for them.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_oven
| The heat comes at you like a hand over your face. The bricks are the size of cattle and every one of them is glowing.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_crater
| A cool summer night, a clean half-moon, and across the water the lights of a city bigger than anything in Druskenvald. In the crater a stone pulses in colours you would swear were not colours.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_bookshelf
| You are the size of a thimble, and the books are walls with titles painted high up where you can't read them. Dust drifts down like snow that has no business being here.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_wedding
| A moonless meadow in flower, lanterns on poles, a long table of food that smells a little too ripe, and twenty guests with animal faces who all turn to look at you at once.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_throne
| The cold is older than the house. Ice furs every stone, and in the blue light the souls go round and round like snow that has learned to cry.
cooldown 20

~ enter:nm_attic
| The attic has swollen the way a bruise swells. The walls are alive with weasels, centipedes and pigeons, all of them very still, all of them watching the pot.
cooldown 20

~ nm_abom_phase2
| The vermin stop murmuring and start screaming, and every wall, beam and board of the attic goes to a boil of teeth.
| Somewhere under the noise, three voices that were never one voice begin to sing at once.
cooldown 0
